      "title": "✏️ PROMPTING GUIDE — How to Write Good Prompts",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "FLUX.2 KLEIN PROMPTING RULES:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n✅ DO:\n• Write like a novelist: Subject → Setting → Details → Light\n• Use technical photo terms: 'shot on Canon R5, 85mm f/1.4'\n• Use power words: 'clean digital file', 'histogram equalization',\n  'gamma correction', 'studio strobe', 'unsharp mask'\n• Put text in quotes: A sign reading \"HELLO\"\n• Be specific: '35-year-old woman with auburn hair'\n\n❌ DON'T:\n• Use vague words: 'beautiful', 'stunning', 'masterpiece'\n• Use SD-style tags: 'best quality, ultra detailed'\n• Use 'trending on artstation' (causes drift)\n• Leave text without quotes (generates gibberish)\n\nFOR KV EDITING (F2/Refiner):\n'Replace [item] with [new item]. Keep pose, expression,\nbackground, and lighting entirely unchanged.'\n\nFOR INPAINTING (F4):\nDescribe ONLY what should appear in the masked area.\nThe model preserves everything outside the mask.\n\nNAG NEGATIVE PROMPT:\nUse with NAG nodes enabled. Example:\n'blurry, low quality, extra fingers, deformed hands'"
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
